      "description": "Enrollment Deposit | Union Commonwealth University Home About Quick Facts News Communications & Marketing University Branding & Logos Department Directory Student Achievement Accreditation Title IX Human Resources Equity in Athletics Disclosure Act Events & Hospitality The Barbourville Home Guard Flag CARES Act Bulldog Life Bulldog Family News Dining Services Housing Clubs & Organizations Campus Activities Technology Campus Safety Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Hazing Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Knox County Tuition-Free Pathway Admissions Events Incoming Freshmen Enrollment Deposit Transfer Students International Students Graduate Graduate International Programs Graduate Education Department of Psychology Online Graduate Degrees Health Sciences Online Online Undergraduate Degrees Cost & Aid Applying for Aid Scholarships & Other Aid Tuition & Fees Estimate Your Cost Scholarships Academics Undergraduate Programs Edna Jenkins Mann School of Nursing Educational Studies Unit Graduate Programs Calendar, Resources & Services Student Support Services Writing Center Accommodation Resource Center Faculty Directory Alumni Giving to Union Homecoming Alumni Events The Mackies QUICK LINKS Academic Calendar Bulldog Store Academic Catalogue Library INFORMATION FOR... Prospective Students Current Students Faculty/Staff Community Alumni RESOURCES WebMail Canvas Physical Plant Work Order Order Business Cards Request a Transcript Order Textbooks MyUnion 3CX Phone System Tech Support Creative Request Form Emergency Text Messages Campus Map enrollment deposit Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Incoming Freshmen Enrollment Deposit After official notification of acceptance to the College is received, all new students are encouraged to submit a non-refundable enrollment deposit of $100. The deposit will be placed on your student account and go toward your overall balance. This deposit should be submitted by May 1 for students entering in the Fall term, and by December 1, for students entering in the Spring term. Students who do not submit an enrollment deposit will not be priority registered for classes. To submit your enrollment deposit, you may contact the Union Commonwealth University Business Office , or click the button below. Pay Enrollment Deposit: APPLY VISIT GIVE ATHLETICS EVENTS STUDENTS PROSPECTIVES FACULTY/STAFF COMMUNITY ALUMNI EMPLOYMENT Your purpose is our mission Privacy Policy Title IX Hazing Accreditation CONTACT US 1 (800) 489-8646 310 College Street Barbourville, KY 40906 QUICK LINKS Home About Bulldog Life Admissions & Aid Academics Calendar © 2026 Union Commonwealth University. All Rights Reserved. Share by:"
