    "https://www.unionky.edu/about/human-resources/employment-opportunities": {
      "title": "job Opportunities",
      "description": "Employment Opportunities | Union Commonwealth University Home About Quick Facts News Communications & Marketing University Branding & Logos Department Directory Student Achievement Accreditation Title IX Human Resources Equity in Athletics Disclosure Act Events & Hospitality The Barbourville Home Guard Flag CARES Act Bulldog Life Bulldog Family News Dining Services Housing Clubs & Organizations Campus Activities Technology Campus Safety Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Hazing Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Knox County Tuition-Free Pathway Admissions Events Incoming Freshmen Enrollment Deposit Transfer Students International Students Graduate Graduate International Programs Graduate Education Department of Psychology Online Graduate Degrees Health Sciences Online Online Undergraduate Degrees Cost & Aid Applying for Aid Scholarships & Other Aid Tuition & Fees Estimate Your Cost Scholarships Academics Undergraduate Programs Edna Jenkins Mann School of Nursing Educational Studies Unit Graduate Programs Calendar, Resources & Services Student Support Services Writing Center Accommodation Resource Center Faculty Directory Alumni Giving to Union Homecoming Alumni Events The Mackies QUICK LINKS Academic Calendar Bulldog Store Academic Catalogue Library INFORMATION FOR... Prospective Students Current Students Faculty/Staff Community Alumni RESOURCES WebMail Canvas Physical Plant Work Order Order Business Cards Request a Transcript Order Textbooks MyUnion 3CX Phone System Tech Support Creative Request Form Emergency Text Messages Campus Map job Opportunities About Human Resources Job Opportunities The procedure for applying for a specific vacancy may vary according to the job title. Please review the vacancy you are interested in to determine the appropriate application procedure. A new application or resume must be submitted for each position of interest. Resumes are accepted only for current vacancies. If you are interested in a particular position, please read the qualifications to determine if you meet the minimum position requirements. Application procedure varies according to job classification (whether faculty or staff), and is noted on the top of the page. If you are presently employed at Union College and interested in a promotion or transfer into any one of the positions listed below, please submit a resume and cover letter to the Human Resources Department, marked confidential. Position vacancies are posted in the Human Resources Department. Regular work hours are Monday through Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. unless otherwise noted. Union Commonwealth University (the \"University\") is committed to maintaining an educational, employment, and business environment free of all forms of discrimination. The University provides full and equal access to its educational services, classes, and programs without regard to and prohibits discrimination based on the protected characteristics of age (40 and older), race, color, national origin, ancestry, religion, sex (including transgender status, gender identity or expression), pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation, and related medical conditions), physical or mental disability, AIDS/HIV status, genetic information (including testing and characteristics), veteran status, uniformed servicemember status, status as a smoker or nonsmoker, medical condition, sexual orientation, marital status, or because an individual is perceived to have one or more of the foregoing characteristics, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local laws. To view current job vacancies at Union College, please click the appropriate button: Faculty Positions Staff Positions Part-Time Staff Positions APPLY VISIT GIVE ATHLETICS EVENTS STUDENTS PROSPECTIVES FACULTY/STAFF COMMUNITY ALUMNI EMPLOYMENT Your purpose is our mission Privacy Policy Title IX Hazing Accreditation CONTACT US 1 (800) 489-8646 310 College Street Barbourville, KY 40906 QUICK LINKS Home About Bulldog Life