      "title": "Faculty PositioNs",
      "description": "Faculty Positions | Union Commonwealth University Home About Quick Facts News Communications & Marketing University Branding & Logos Department Directory Student Achievement Accreditation Title IX Human Resources Equity in Athletics Disclosure Act Events & Hospitality The Barbourville Home Guard Flag CARES Act Bulldog Life Bulldog Family News Dining Services Housing Clubs & Organizations Campus Activities Technology Campus Safety Annual Security & Fire Safety Report Hazing Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Knox County Tuition-Free Pathway Admissions Events Incoming Freshmen Enrollment Deposit Transfer Students International Students Graduate Graduate International Programs Graduate Education Department of Psychology Online Graduate Degrees Health Sciences Online Online Undergraduate Degrees Cost & Aid Applying for Aid Scholarships & Other Aid Tuition & Fees Estimate Your Cost Scholarships Academics Undergraduate Programs Edna Jenkins Mann School of Nursing Educational Studies Unit Graduate Programs Calendar, Resources & Services Student Support Services Writing Center Accommodation Resource Center Faculty Directory Alumni Giving to Union Homecoming Alumni Events The Mackies QUICK LINKS Academic Calendar Bulldog Store Academic Catalogue Library INFORMATION FOR... Prospective Students Current Students Faculty/Staff Community Alumni RESOURCES WebMail Canvas Physical Plant Work Order Order Business Cards Request a Transcript Order Textbooks MyUnion 3CX Phone System Tech Support Creative Request Form Emergency Text Messages Campus Map Faculty PositioNs About Human Resources Job Opportunities Faculty Positions Academic Faculty and Administrative Positions Mission : To serve the academic needs of a diverse community of undergraduate, graduate, and continuing education students in a dynamic, personal environment that promotes intellectual, spiritual, and physical enrichment of students, faculty, and staff and the economic growth and health of our Appalachian region. Union Commonwealth University challenges students to make learning connections, to master key competencies, to achieve a diversity of perspectives, to experience intellectual and ethical growth, to make meaningful choices, to practice creative problem solving, to pursue spiritual growth and integrity of character, and to establish a habit of lifelong learning. The college also expects students to develop a life philosophy; intentionally seeks to produce graduates who see being educated as a quality of mind; and enables members of the faculty to significantly improve student learning. In our effort to achieve these goals, we seek persons of integrity, vision, intellectual curiosity, and devotion to student learning to fill the positions listed below. Application Procedures Review of Faculty applications will begin immediately and continue until the vacancy is filled. Interested candidates should send cover letter, resume, and list of references with phone numbers to: Human Resources Union Commonwealth University 310 College Street, CPO Box D-3 Barbourville, KY 40906 Email applications can be sent to tlsmith@unionky.edu Successful candidates must complete a background check, submit official academic transcripts, and provide evidence of authorization to work in the United States. Union Commonwealth University (the \"University\") is committed to maintaining an educational, employment, and business environment free of all forms of discrimination. The University provides full and equal access to its educational services, classes, and programs without regard to and prohibits discrimination based on the protected characteristics of age (40 and older), race, color, national origin, ancestry, religion, sex (including transgender status, gender identity or expression), pregnancy (including childbirth, lactation, and related medical conditions), physical or mental disability, AIDS/HIV status, genetic information (including testing and characteristics), veteran status, uniformed servicemember status, status as a smoker or nonsmoker, medical condition, sexual orientation, marital status, or because an individual is perceived to have one or more of the foregoing characteristics, or any other status protected by federal, state, or local laws. Current Positions Available: Assistant Professor of Biology APPLY VISIT GIVE ATHLETICS EVENTS STUDENTS PROSPECTIVES FACULTY/STAFF COMMUNITY ALUMNI EMPLOYMENT Your purpose is our mission Privacy Policy Title IX Hazing Accreditation CONTACT US 1 (800) 489-8646 310 College Street Barbourville, KY 40906 QUICK LINKS Home About Bulldog Life Admissions & Aid Academics Calendar © 2026 Union Commonwealth University. All Rights Reserved. Share by:"
